  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">48 Hours Response to Amhara Crisis (MPCA, WASH, Health and Protection)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ltpgtSave the Children (SC) proposes integrated life-saving assistance to conflict-affected communities in North Shewa and the Oromia Special Zone of the Amhara region. The project will focus on providing essential support, including cash assistance, emergency shelter and Non-Food Items (NFIs), water, sanitation, and hygiene (WASH) services, disease outbreak prevention, and protection services. The project will reach vulnerable communities, including internally displaced persons (IDPs), returnees, and host communities. It will address various needs through comprehensive interventions.&#xA0;For food security and livelihoods, the project will provide multipurpose cash assistance and capacity building training for targeted households, committee members, and communities. Additionally, it will strengthen existing health systems to ensure continued access to primary healthcare services, including outbreak preparedness and response.&#xA0;The project will also address WASH needs by rehabilitating water sources, building local capacity for facility maintenance, and constructing or rehabilitating sanitation facilities with hygiene promotion activities and essential hygiene item provision.&#xA0;Furthermore, the project addresses protection concerns and gender-based violence (GBV) through case management, mental health and psychosocial services for survivors, community awareness sessions, and relevant training to effectively handle GBV cases. ltbrgtltbrgtlt/pgt</narrative>
  </description>
